			"id":"8ad1a860621d2d76",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# SESSION 1 — MY FAVORITE OBJECT\n**Conversation Foundation | A1 | 90 minutes**\n\n**Speaking Goal:** I can describe an object and explain why I like it.\n\n## PART 1 — READING & INSIGHT\n\n### Reading: My Small Blue Bag\n\nMy name is Lan. I have many things in my room, but my favorite thing is my small blue bag. I use it every day. It is not new, but it is clean and strong. I bought it at a shop near my house. It was not expensive. I like the color because blue is my favorite color.\n\nEvery morning, I put my phone, keys, wallet, and a small notebook in the bag. I carry it to work. On the bus, I keep it on my lap. At work, I put it next to my desk. My friends sometimes say, “You always have that bag!” I smile and say, “Yes, I do. It is easy to carry.”\n\nI also have a watch. It is black and very simple. My father gave it to me. I wear it when I go to work. I have a family photo in my wallet, too. The photo is small, but it is special to me. When I look at it, I think about my family.\n\nThe bag, the watch, and the photo are different. I use them in different ways. They are part of my everyday life. I do not need expensive things to be happy.\n\n### Insight — Don't Just Name It. Describe It!\n\nKhi nói về một đồ vật, đừng chỉ nói tên. Hãy bổ sung màu sắc, công dụng và lý do bạn thích nó.\n\n**Basic:**\n\nI have a bag.\n\n**More Natural:**\n\nI have a small blue bag. I use it every day because it's easy to carry.\n\n**Remember:**\n\nObject → Appearance → Use → Feeling\n\nĐồ vật → Đặc điểm → Công dụng → Cảm nhận\n\n## PART 2 — VOCABULARY & COLLOCATIONS\n\n| Expression | Nghĩa tiếng Việt | Natural Example | Dịch ví dụ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| my favorite thing | món đồ yêu thích | My favorite thing is my watch. | Món đồ tôi thích nhất là chiếc đồng hồ. |\n| use it every day | sử dụng mỗi ngày | I use my phone every day. | Tôi dùng điện thoại mỗi ngày. |\n| carry it with me | mang theo bên mình | I carry my bag with me. | Tôi mang túi theo bên mình. |\n| easy to use | dễ sử dụng | This phone is easy to use. | Chiếc điện thoại này dễ sử dụng. |\n| easy to carry | dễ mang theo | My bag is small and easy to carry. | Túi của tôi nhỏ và dễ mang theo. |\n| a gift from… | món quà từ… | This watch is a gift from my dad. | Chiếc đồng hồ này là quà bố tặng tôi. |\n| look nice | trông đẹp | Your new bag looks nice. | Chiếc túi mới của bạn trông đẹp đấy. |\n| work well | hoạt động tốt | My old phone still works well. | Điện thoại cũ của tôi vẫn hoạt động tốt. |\n| special to me | đặc biệt đối với tôi | This photo is special to me. | Bức ảnh này rất đặc biệt với tôi. |\n| remind me of… | làm tôi nhớ đến… | This photo reminds me of my family. | Bức ảnh này làm tôi nhớ đến gia đình. |\n\n## PART 3 — SENTENCE FRAMEWORK\n\n| Function | Framework | Nghĩa tiếng Việt |\n|---|---|---|\n| Introduce | My favorite thing is… | Món đồ tôi thích nhất là… |\n| Name | I have a… | Tôi có một… |\n| Describe | It's small / big / old / new. | Nó nhỏ / lớn / cũ / mới. |\n| Color | It's black / white / blue. | Nó màu đen / trắng / xanh. |\n| Origin | I got it from… | Tôi nhận nó từ… |\n| Use | I use it to… | Tôi dùng nó để… |\n| Feeling | I like it because… | Tôi thích nó vì… |\n| Meaning | It's special to me because… | Nó đặc biệt với tôi vì… |\n\n### Example — Building an Answer\n\n**Question:** What's your favorite thing?\n\n**Level 1:** My watch.\n\n**Level 2:** My favorite thing is my watch.\n\n**Level 3:** It's small and black.\n\n**Level 4:** My dad gave it to me.\n\n**Level 5:** I like it because it's special to me.\n\n## PART 4 — APPLYING EXERCISES\n\n### Exercise 1 — Reading Check\n\nĐọc bài và trả lời bằng câu ngắn.\n\n1. What color is Lan's bag?\n\n   Answer: __________________________________\n\n2. Where did she buy it?\n\n   Answer: __________________________________\n\n3. What does she put in her bag?\n\n   Answer: __________________________________\n\n4. Who gave Lan her watch?\n\n   Answer: __________________________________\n\n5. Why is the family photo special?\n\n   Answer: __________________________________\n\n### Exercise 2 — Upgrade the Sentence\n\nThêm chi tiết để câu tự nhiên và đầy đủ hơn.\n\n**Example:**\n\nBasic: I have a phone.\n\nBetter: I have a black phone. I use it every day.\n\n**Your turn:**\n\n1. I have a bag.\n\n   Better: __________________________________\n\n2. My watch is old.\n\n   Better: __________________________________\n\n3. I like my phone.\n\n   Better: __________________________________\n\n4. I have a photo.\n\n   Better: __________________________________\n\n5. This gift is special.\n\n   Better: __________________________________\n\n**Useful words:** black, small, useful, nice, my family, my friend, every day, easy to use.\n\n### Exercise 3 — Ask Your Partner\n\nLàm việc theo cặp. Student A hỏi, Student B trả lời. Sau đó đổi vai.\n\n| Question | Nghĩa tiếng Việt |\n|---|---|\n| What's your favorite thing? | Đồ vật yêu thích của bạn là gì? |\n| What color is it? | Nó màu gì? |\n| Is it new or old? | Nó mới hay cũ? |\n| Where did you get it? | Bạn có nó từ đâu? |\n| Do you use it every day? | Bạn có dùng nó mỗi ngày không? |\n| Why do you like it? | Tại sao bạn thích nó? |\n\n**Challenge:** Không trả lời một từ. Hãy trả lời ít nhất 2 câu.\n\n## PART 5 — FINAL SUM-UP EXERCISE\n\n### SHOW & TELL — 30–60 SECONDS\n\n**Task:** Choose one object and tell your partner about it.\n\nChọn một đồ vật và giới thiệu cho bạn cùng lớp.\n\n**Object Ideas:** Phone, watch, bag, book, photo, laptop, headphones, shoes, keychain.\n\n**My Speaking Notes**\n\n1. Object: ____________________\n2. Color: ____________________\n3. Size: ____________________\n4. Where I got it: ____________________\n5. How I use it: ____________________\n6. Why I like it: ____________________\n\n**Speaking Challenge**\n\n- Introduce the object.\n- Describe its color and size.\n- Explain how you use it.\n- Say why you like it.\n- Answer two questions from your partner.\n\n### SELF-CHECK\n\n- [ ] I can name my favorite object.\n- [ ] I can describe its color and size.\n- [ ] I can explain how I use it.\n- [ ] I can explain why I like it.\n- [ ] I can speak for 30–60 seconds.\n\n**TAKEAWAY**\n\nDon't just say: “I have a bag.”\n\nSay: “I have a small blue bag. I use it every day, and I really like it.”",
