			"id":"a633b6c5353cf65e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# SESSION 2 — THE STORY BEHIND IT\n**Storytelling Foundation | A1 | 90 minutes**\n\n**Speaking Goal:** I can tell a short story about a special object.\n\n## PART 1 — READING & INSIGHT\n\n### Reading: A Photo from My Mom\n\nI have a small family photo. It is very special to me. My mother gave it to me last year, before I moved to a new city for work. In the photo, my mother, my father, and my little sister are smiling. We are in our old home. I keep the photo in my wallet.\n\nOne Monday morning, I got ready for work. I looked for my wallet, but I could not find it. I checked my bag, my desk, and my bed. It was not there. I felt worried because my money, my cards, and my family photo were in the wallet.\n\nI called my friend Mai. She came to my room and helped me look for it. After ten minutes, she found the wallet under a book on my table. I was so happy! I said, “Thank you, Mai!” She smiled and said, “No problem.”\n\nI opened my wallet and looked at the photo. It was still there. I felt very happy and calm. The wallet is useful, but the photo is more important to me. It reminds me of my family and my home. Now I always put my wallet in the same place.\n\n### Insight — Every Object Has a Story\n\nMột đồ vật không cần đắt tiền để có ý nghĩa.\n\nMột câu chuyện ngắn thường trả lời:\n\n- Bạn có món đồ đó khi nào?\n- Ai đã tặng hoặc đưa nó cho bạn?\n- Chuyện gì đã xảy ra?\n- Bạn cảm thấy thế nào?\n- Tại sao bạn vẫn giữ nó?\n\n**Basic:**\n\nMy mom gave me a photo. I like it.\n\n**More Natural:**\n\nMy mom gave me this photo last year. One day, I lost my wallet, and I was really worried. Luckily, my friend found it. I was so happy because the photo was still there.\n\n**Remember:**\n\nObject → When / Who → Event → Feeling → Ending\n\nĐồ vật → Khi nào / Ai → Sự việc → Cảm xúc → Kết thúc\n\n## PART 2 — VOCABULARY & COLLOCATIONS\n\n| Expression | Nghĩa tiếng Việt | Natural Example | Dịch ví dụ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| a special gift | món quà đặc biệt | This is a special gift from my mom. | Đây là món quà đặc biệt mẹ tặng tôi. |\n| a long time ago | từ rất lâu rồi | I got this book a long time ago. | Tôi có cuốn sách này từ lâu rồi. |\n| on my birthday | vào ngày sinh nhật | I got this watch on my birthday. | Tôi nhận chiếc đồng hồ này vào sinh nhật. |\n| when I was a child | khi tôi còn nhỏ | I got this toy when I was a child. | Tôi có món đồ chơi này khi còn nhỏ. |\n| give it to me | đưa / tặng nó cho tôi | My sister gave it to me. | Chị tôi đã tặng nó cho tôi. |\n| look for something | tìm kiếm thứ gì | I looked for my phone. | Tôi đã tìm điện thoại của mình. |\n| lose something | làm mất thứ gì | I lost my keys yesterday. | Hôm qua tôi làm mất chìa khóa. |\n| find something | tìm thấy thứ gì | I found my bag under the table. | Tôi tìm thấy túi dưới bàn. |\n| feel really worried | cảm thấy rất lo lắng | I felt really worried. | Tôi đã cảm thấy rất lo lắng. |\n| keep it safe | giữ gìn cẩn thận | I keep this photo safe. | Tôi giữ bức ảnh này rất cẩn thận. |\n\n### Mini Feeling Bank\n\n| Feeling | Nghĩa | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| happy | vui | I was so happy. — Tôi đã rất vui. |\n| sad | buồn | I felt sad. — Tôi đã thấy buồn. |\n| worried | lo lắng | I was worried. — Tôi đã rất lo. |\n| surprised | bất ngờ | I was surprised. — Tôi đã bất ngờ. |\n| excited | hào hứng | I was really excited. — Tôi đã rất hào hứng. |\n| thankful | biết ơn | I felt thankful. — Tôi đã cảm thấy biết ơn. |\n\n## PART 3 — SENTENCE FRAMEWORK\n\n| Story Step | Framework | Nghĩa tiếng Việt |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Object | I want to talk about my… | Tôi muốn kể về… |\n| 2. Time | I got it… years ago. | Tôi có nó cách đây… năm. |\n| 3. Person | My… gave it to me. | …đã tặng nó cho tôi. |\n| 4. Context | It was my birthday / first day at work. | Đó là sinh nhật / ngày đầu đi làm của tôi. |\n| 5. Event | One day, I… | Một ngày nọ, tôi… |\n| 6. Reaction | I felt… | Tôi đã cảm thấy… |\n| 7. Ending | In the end,… | Cuối cùng thì… |\n| 8. Meaning | I still keep it because… | Tôi vẫn giữ nó vì… |\n\n### Example — From Object to Story\n\n**Object**\n\nI have a small watch.\n\n**Time / Person**\n\nMy dad gave it to me two years ago.\n\n**Event**\n\nOne day, I left it at home.\n\n**Reaction**\n\nI was worried because I really liked it.\n\n**Ending**\n\nLuckily, I found it on my desk. I still wear it every day.\n\n## PART 4 — APPLYING EXERCISES\n\n### Exercise 1 — Reading Check\n\nTrả lời dựa trên bài đọc.\n\n1. What object is special to the speaker?\n\n   Answer: __________________________________\n\n2. Who gave her the photo?\n\n   Answer: __________________________________\n\n3. What did she lose?\n\n   Answer: __________________________________\n\n4. Who helped her?\n\n   Answer: __________________________________\n\n5. Where was the wallet?\n\n   Answer: __________________________________\n\n6. How did she feel when she found it?\n\n   Answer: __________________________________\n\n### Exercise 2 — Action + Reaction\n\nNối một hành động với cảm xúc phù hợp, sau đó viết câu.\n\n| Action | Possible Reaction |\n|---|---|\n| Your friend gives you a gift. | happy / excited |\n| You lose your phone. | worried / sad |\n| You find an old family photo. | happy / surprised |\n| Your mother gives you a watch. | happy / thankful |\n| You find your lost bag. | happy / relieved |\n\n**Example:**\n\nAction: My friend gave me a gift.\n\nReaction: I was so happy.\n\n**Your Turn**\n\n1. My mom gave me ____________________.\n\n   I felt ____________________.\n\n2. One day, I lost ____________________.\n\n   I was ____________________.\n\n3. I found ____________________.\n\n   I felt ____________________.\n\n4. My friend helped me ____________________.\n\n   I was ____________________.\n\n### Exercise 3 — Build a Little Story\n\nChọn một story cue dưới đây và hoàn thành 4–5 câu.\n\n**Story A — A Birthday Gift**\n\nYour friend gave you a gift on your birthday.\n\nBạn được bạn bè tặng quà vào sinh nhật.\n\n**Story B — My Lost Phone**\n\nYou lost your phone at a café. A worker found it.\n\nBạn làm mất điện thoại ở quán cà phê. Một nhân viên tìm thấy nó.\n\n**Story C — An Old Photo**\n\nYou found an old family photo while cleaning your room.\n\nBạn tìm thấy một bức ảnh gia đình cũ khi dọn phòng.\n\n**Story D — A Gift from My Dad**\n\nYour dad gave you a watch before your first day at work.\n\nBố tặng bạn một chiếc đồng hồ trước ngày đầu tiên đi làm.\n\n**Story Builder**\n\n1. I have a ____________________.\n2. I got it ____________________.\n3. One day, ____________________.\n4. I felt ____________________.\n5. I still keep it because ____________________.\n\n**Pair Practice:** Kể cho bạn cùng lớp trong 30 giây. Bạn nghe hỏi thêm: “What happened next?” hoặc “How did you feel?”\n\n## PART 5 — FINAL SUM-UP EXERCISE\n\n### A LITTLE STORY ABOUT MY OBJECT — 30–60 SECONDS\n\nChọn một đồ vật có ý nghĩa với bạn.\n\nCó thể là:\n\n- a gift from your family\n- your first phone\n- an old photo\n- a favorite book\n- a birthday present\n- something you lost and found\n\n**My Story Notes**\n\n| Question | My Answer |\n|---|---|\n| What is it? | __________________ |\n| Who gave it to you? | __________________ |\n| When did you get it? | __________________ |\n| What happened? | __________________ |\n| How did you feel? | __________________ |\n| Why is it special? | __________________ |\n\n### Speaking Challenge\n\nKể một câu chuyện 30–60 giây.\n\nYêu cầu:\n\n1. Introduce your object.\n2. Say when or where you got it.\n3. Tell one small event.\n4. Describe your feeling.\n5. Explain why it is special.\n\n**Không đọc script. Chỉ sử dụng keywords.**\n\n### Partner Follow-up Questions\n\n- Who gave it to you? — Ai đã tặng bạn?\n- When did you get it? — Bạn nhận nó khi nào?\n- What happened next? — Sau đó chuyện gì xảy ra?\n- How did you feel? — Bạn cảm thấy thế nào?\n- Do you still have it? — Bạn vẫn còn giữ nó chứ?\n\n### SELF-CHECK\n\n- [ ] I can introduce an object.\n- [ ] I can say when I got it.\n- [ ] I can explain what happened.\n- [ ] I can describe my feelings.\n- [ ] I can tell a 30–60 second story.\n- [ ] I can answer simple follow-up questions.\n\n**TAKEAWAY**\n\nDon't just say: “This photo is important.”\n\nSay: “My mom gave me this photo. I got it last year. It reminds me of my family, so I keep it in my wallet.”",
